---
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import chrisPhoto from '../assets/team/chris-mcleod.jpg';
import alexPhoto from '../assets/team/alex-maclean.jpg';
---

<Base
  title="About — BluHeron Interactive"
  description="BluHeron Interactive is a creative technology studio in London & Hamilton, Ontario — co-founded by Christopher McLeod and Alex MacLean, guided by community collaboration and the 5 Rs."
>
  <section class="wrap head">
    <p class="kicker">About us</p>
    <h1 class="display">Builds cities, communities, <em class="clay">connections</em>.</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap story">
    <p>
      Partnership, community collaboration, co-creation, and just having fun and being creative
      while igniting community interaction is our focus — and very exciting to us.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our blend of arts-based research for public engagement and community feedback focuses on
      a principles-based approach where honesty, respect, equality, fairness, and courage are
      our guides. We work to provide supportive time and space for diverse, equity-seeking
      people to feel empowered to engage in our interactive experiences. Together, we create
      through lived experiences following the <a href={withBase('/values/')}>5 Rs</a> — Respect, Relevance,
      Responsibility, Reciprocity, and Relationality.
    </p>
    <p>
      That work has grown. Today BluHeron is three practices with one mission: immersive
      installations co-created with communities, <a href={withBase('/beacbeac/')}>beacbeac</a> — our
      platform making public places accessible to everyone — and digital services that keep
      arts organizations' own doors open online. As a team, we have had the opportunity to
      create with amazing partners on arts-based community development projects across Ontario,
      and we are always excited to meet new project partners, collaborators, and friends.
      <a href={withBase('/contact/')}>Let's talk.</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap team">
    <h2>Our team</h2>
    <div class="people">
      <article class="person reveal">
        <Image src={chrisPhoto} alt="Portrait of Christopher McLeod" width={600} widths={[300, 600]} sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 300px" />
        <h3>Christopher McLeod</h3>
        <p class="role">Co-founder &middot; Artistic director</p>
        <p>
          A freelance artist and artistic director for three decades, Chris has led 24
          community-engaged public art projects across Ontario, with a BA in Studio Art from
          McMaster and an MFA from Emily Carr University focused on social practice and
          community interaction. His work has always been about creating opportunities for
          people to connect in positive and meaningful ways — art just sort of happened along
          the way.
        </p>
        <p class="land">
          Chris is of settler ancestry, living on the traditional territory of the
          Haudenosaunee, Wendat, and Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="person reveal">
        <Image src={alexPhoto} alt="Portrait of Alex MacLean" width={600} widths={[300, 600]} sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 300px" />
        <h3>Alex MacLean</h3>
        <p class="role">Co-founder &middot; Creative technologist</p>
        <p>
          An immersive media artist and developer, Alex builds the technology behind
          BluHeron's work — from generative audiovisual installations to the beacbeac platform
          and its accessibility-audited apps and console. Sound, light, and code: experiences
          that listen back.
        </p>
        <p class="land">
          <a href="https://alexmaclean.ca" rel="noopener">alexmaclean.ca &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band advisors">
    <div class="wrap inner">
      <div class="lead">
        <h2>Our advisors</h2>
        <p>
          We are privileged to work with several diverse advisors in the development and
          delivery of our projects. We commit to including our advisors from the start of each
          project, with check-ins throughout delivery. Focusing on decolonizing, diversity,
          and inclusivity requires many voices and perspectives to be embedded in the
          activations we develop and deliver.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cols">
        <article class="reveal">
          <h3>Colina Phillips</h3>
          <p>
            A singer, filmmaker, and writer whose creative energy has spanned five decades —
            from session singing and a Gold Record with Sway to writing, producing, and
            directing <em>Making Change</em>, which premiered at the Toronto International
            Film Festival. Colina brought her lens to two BluHeron public productions,
            <a href={withBase('/work/jump-around/')}>Jump Around</a> and Our Home, Your Home.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="reveal">
          <h3>Kawennakon Bonnie Whitlow</h3>
          <p>
            Mohawk, Bear Clan. Kawennakon has been revitalizing cultural practices and
            connecting to ancestral spiritual ceremonies, traditional dances, and songs since
            her early 20s. A second-language speaker of Kanyen'kéha, she is a scholar, author,
            lecturer, community organizer, activist, artist, and actress — and has been
            learning, teaching, and advocating for ancestral language revitalization for
            decades.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactCTA heading="New partners, collaborators &amp; friends — <em>let’s talk</em>." />
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 80px) clamp(24px, 4vw, 36px);
  }

  .head em.clay {
    color: var(--clay);
  }

  .story {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 22px;
    padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 7vw, 72px);
  }

  .story p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  .team {
    padding-block: 0 clamp(56px, 8vw, 88px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 40px;
  }

  .team h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .people {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px);
  }

  .person {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .person img {
    width: min(300px, 100%);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .person h3 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }

  .role {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--clay);
  }

  .person p:not(.role) {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .person .land {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .advisors .inner {
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 88px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 44px;
  }

  .lead {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .lead h2 {
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .lead p {
    color: var(--band-ink-2);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px);
  }

  .cols article {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--band-line);
    padding-top: 24px;
  }

  .cols h3 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }

  .cols p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--band-ink-2);
  }
</style>
